\left( x^2 - 2xy + y^2 \right) + (2y^2 + 2xy + \sqrt{2}y^2) &= 6 \\
\left( x - y \right)^2 + (y + \sqrt{2}y)^2 &= 6 \\
\frac{(x-y)^2}{6} + \frac{(y+\sqrt{2}y)^2}{6} &= 1.
\end{align*}This represents a circle with radius $\sqrt{6}$ and center $\left( 0, -\sqrt{2} \right)$.
