 Consider the units number of $1^n$ for $n = 1, 2, \cdots$. Note that all of them is equal to 1, so $S(1^n) = 1$, and their sum is $n \times 1 = n$, where $S(\cdot)$ denotes the sum of the digits. Therefore, the units digit of $17^{18}$ is the same as the units digit of $1^n$ where $n = 18$, which is 1. Similarly, the units digit of $19^{0}$ and $18^{0}$ are 1 and 1, respectively. Thus, the units digit of $16^{17} \times 17^{ NJ40} \times 18^{19}$ is the units digit of $1^{17} \times 1^{18} \times 1^{0}$, which is $\boxed{1}$.
